{"book":24,"chapter":45,"context":{"chapter":45,"title":"A Word for Baruch","summary":"A short message to Baruch, Jeremiah's scribe, from the year he wrote the scroll: Baruch groans of grief upon grief. God answers that He is tearing down what He built, so Baruch should not seek great things for himself, but God will give him his life wherever he goes.","background":"Baruch son of Neriah came from a prominent family; his brother Seraiah was a royal officer (51:59). Dated to Jehoiakim's fourth year (605 BC), this note belongs in time with chapter 36 but is placed here, after the flight to Egypt. It shows God's personal care for a faithful helper amid national collapse.","customs":[{"term":"Thy life… for a prey","verses":"45:5","note":"A soldier's saying: to escape with your life as your only plunder. Ebed-melech received the same promise (39:18)."}],"watchFor":["Baruch's lament echoes Jeremiah's own (v. 3).","God's own loss: 'that which I have built will I break down' (v. 4).","'Seekest thou great things for thyself? seek them not' (v. 5)."],"connections":["Jeremiah 36:4","Jeremiah 51:59","Jeremiah 39:18"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["הַדָּבָר","hadavar","H1697","HTd/Ncmsa","the word"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["דִּבֶּר","diber","H1696","HVpp3ms","he spoke"],["יִרְמְיָהוּ","yirmeyahu","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["הַנָּבִיא","hanavi'","H5030","HTd/Ncmsa","the prophet"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["בָּרוּךְ","barukh","H1263","HNpm","Baruch"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["נֵרִיָּה","neriyah","H5374","HNpm","Neriah"],["בְּכָתְבוֹ","bekhatevo","H3789","HR/Vqcc/Sp3ms","when wrote he"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הַדְּבָרִים","hadevarim","H1697","HTd/Ncmpa","the words"],["הָאֵלֶּה","ha'eleh","H428","HTd/Tm","<the> these"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["סֵפֶר","sefer","H5612","HNcmsa","a scroll"],["מִפִּי","mipi","H6310","HR/Ncmsc","from [the] mouth of"],["יִרְמְיָהוּ","yirmeyahu","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["בַּשָּׁנָה","bas